/-! # Globalization of labelled coordinate boundaries

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Travaux de Gabber, Expose VIII 4.1.2--4.1.4(i),
Remark 4.2.2(i), and Lemma 4.2.9, printed pp. 117--121
(blueprint: lem-trf-labelled-coordinate-boundary-globalization).

Closed subschemes are represented by their quasi-coherent ideals. Infima give unions,
suprema give scheme-theoretic intersections, and radical gives the reduced structure.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Labelled coordinate hyperplanes globalize to the stated regular components and boundary.
Source: ILO, Expose VIII 4.1.2--4.1.4(i), Remark 4.2.2(i), and Lemma 4.2.9,
printed pp. 117--121 (blueprint: lem-trf-labelled-coordinate-boundary-globalization).

Proof:
1. At each point, the actual etale chart gives a flat local map from the ambient stalk
   to the regular chart stalk. Flat descent gives regularity of the ambient stalk.
   For each nonempty label use the quotient by its assigned parameter and the same descent
   (lem-trf-finite-intersection-etale-stalk-model, lem-weil-pbc-flat-under-regular,
   lem-sfb-transverse-prime-ideal-parameters).
2. The closed scheme E is Noetherian and regular. Its finitely many irreducible components
   are disjoint and clopen, and inherit regularity (rem-pc-regular-normal). At a point of E
   just one survives in the chart, so refining E into these components preserves the distinct
   labelled coordinate equations. The F_a are integral because reduced and irreducible.
3. Intersections of the refined family have ideals generated by distinct chosen parameters,
   or the unit ideal when one member is absent. Descend regularity and component codimension
   using lem-trf-etale-regular-intersection-descent, including the empty intersection.
4. The parameter-quotient dimension formula and etale invariance of local dimension give
   dim O_Y = dim O_intersection + number of chosen members at every intersection point
   (lem-sc-etale-local-dimension, lem-weil-pbc-etale-scheme-base-change).
5. Etale pullbacks of C and D are reduced. Their local ideals are products of the specified
   distinct parameter primes; for D this follows by intersecting the label primes.
   The products are nonzerodivisors, including the empty product 1
   (lem-trf-etale-reduced-cartier-descent, lem-weil-pbc-reduced-induced-closed-subscheme,
   lem-sfb-transverse-prime-ideal-parameters).
6. The flat local stalk map is faithfully flat and its affine spectrum is an fpqc cover.
   Reflect the Cartier ideal down to the target stalk and spread its generator near the point
   (lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-hom-faithfully-flat, lem-trf-fpqc-cartier-ideal-reflection,
   lem-sfb-stalk-nonzerodivisor-cartier-spreading). Thus C and D are effective Cartier.
7. The actual etale charts and their parameter-product equations give normal crossings for C
   (def-trf-normal-crossings-divisor).
8. Different refined members are incomparable: distinct E components are disjoint, and
   distinct original labels have incomparable parameter primes locally. A finite union of
   irreducible closed subsets with no containments has exactly these components. Uniqueness
   of reduced induced structures identifies their scheme structures. Together with steps 3--6
   this is def-trf-strict-normal-crossings-boundary.
9. Each refined member lies in a component of C. A strict containment would give a chain of
   length two up to a component of Y, since an effective Cartier divisor contains no nonempty
   open subset. This contradicts its codimension one from step 3
   (lem-sc-noetherian-closed-subset-finite-components, lem-pc-cartier-divisor-nowhere-dense).
   Hence D is a union of components of C. Empty schemes and empty families give the same
   assertions with empty component lists and unit ideals.
-/
theorem labelled_coordinate_boundary_globalization
    (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian Y] {m : ℕ}
    (E C D : Y.IdealSheafData) (F : Fin m → Y.IdealSheafData)
    (hE : E.radical = E) (hC : C.radical = C)
    (hF : ∀ a : Fin m, (F a).radical = F a)
    (hirr : ∀ a : Fin m, IrreducibleSpace (F a).subscheme)
    (hdistinct : Function.Injective F)
    (hEC : C ≤ E) (hFC : ∀ a : Fin m, C ≤ F a)
    (hD : D = (E ⊓ ⨅ a : Fin m, F a).radical)
    (hcharts : ∀ y : Y,
      ∃ (V : Scheme.{u}) (v : V ⟶ Y) (z : V), Etale v ∧ v z = y ∧
        ∃ (hN : IsNoetherianRing (V.presheaf.stalk z))
          (d : ℕ) (s : Fin d → V.presheaf.stalk z) (K : Finset (Fin d))
          (label : Fin (m + 1) → Option (Fin d)),
          IsRegularLocalRing (V.presheaf.stalk z) ∧
          @IsLocalRing.IsRegularSystemOfParameters _ _ _ hN
            (List.ofFn s) ∧
          (∀ (a b : Fin (m + 1)) (i : Fin d),
            label a = some i → label b = some i → a = b) ∧
          (∀ a : Fin (m + 1),
            match label a with
            | none =>
                HilbertSamuel.stalkIdeal
                  ((Fin.cons (α := fun _ ↦ Y.IdealSheafData) E F a).comap v) z = ⊤
            | some i => i ∈ K ∧
                HilbertSamuel.stalkIdeal
                  ((Fin.cons (α := fun _ ↦ Y.IdealSheafData) E F a).comap v) z =
                  Ideal.span {s i}) ∧
          (HilbertSamuel.stalkIdeal (C.comap v) z).radical =
            Ideal.span {∏ i ∈ K, s i} ∧
          (∀ J : Finset (Fin d), J ⊆ K →
            IsRegularScheme
              (Spec (.of (V.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ Ideal.span (s '' (J : Set (Fin d)))))) ∧
            ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum (V.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ Ideal.span (s '' (J : Set (Fin d)))),
              closure ({p} : Set (PrimeSpectrum
                (V.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ Ideal.span (s '' (J : Set (Fin d)))))) ∈
                  irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum
                    (V.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ Ideal.span (s '' (J : Set (Fin d))))) →
                Order.height (PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk
                  (Ideal.span (s '' (J : Set (Fin d))))) p) = (J.card : ℕ∞))) :
    IsRegularScheme Y ∧ IsRegularScheme E.subscheme ∧
    (∀ a : Fin m, IsRegularScheme (F a).subscheme) ∧
    C.IsInvertible ∧ D.IsInvertible ∧ C.IsNormalCrossingsDivisor ∧
    (∃ (n : ℕ) (G : Fin n → Y.IdealSheafData),
      (∀ b : Fin n, (G b).radical = G b ∧ (G b).support ≤ E.support ∧
        IsClopen (E.subschemeι ⁻¹' ((G b).support : Set Y))) ∧
      Function.Injective (fun b : Fin n ↦ (G b).support) ∧
      Set.range (fun b : Fin n ↦ (G b).support : Fin n → Set Y) =
        (fun Z : Set E.subscheme ↦ E.subschemeι '' Z) ''
          irreducibleComponents E.subscheme ∧
      (∀ b c : Fin n, b ≠ c → Disjoint (G b).support (G c).support) ∧
      (fun Z : Set D.subscheme ↦ D.subschemeι '' Z) ''
          irreducibleComponents D.subscheme =
        Set.range (fun b : Fin n ↦ (G b).support : Fin n → Set Y) ∪
          Set.range (fun a : Fin m ↦ (F a).support : Fin m → Set Y) ∧
      (∀ J : Finset (Fin n ⊕ Fin m),
        IsRegularScheme (⨆ i ∈ J, Sum.elim G F i).subscheme ∧
        ∀ p : (⨆ i ∈ J, Sum.elim G F i).subscheme,
          closure ({p} : Set (⨆ i ∈ J, Sum.elim G F i).subscheme) ∈
              irreducibleComponents (⨆ i ∈ J, Sum.elim G F i).subscheme →
            Order.coheight ((⨆ i ∈ J, Sum.elim G F i).subschemeι p) = (J.card : ℕ∞))) ∧
    IsStrictNormalCrossingsBoundary D ∧ IsUnionOfIrreducibleComponents D C := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
